  <prompt>
    Unify the born-in-editor path (FR-09). Documents drafted from scratch (no source `.docx`) MUST feed
    the SAME operation/patch model: their initial content becomes an INSERT-EVERYTHING operation set
    applied onto an EMPTY shadow package by `ComposeShadowPatchEngine` — so NO parallel full-render
    export path remains. Modify the BFF save path
    (`src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs`) to route born-in-editor saves
    through the Patch Engine, and reconcile/remove the client full-render path
    `buildContentModel` in `src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/utils/docxBridge.ts:397+`
    so the client emits the same operation log for born-in-editor as for edit-existing. Client fetches
    use `@spaarke/auth` (ADR-028). This is a MODIFY consolidating a parallel path into the unified model,
    not new surface. If any born-in-editor formatting cannot be expressed as an operation set, surface it
    rather than silently keeping a second render path.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Full-stack developer: .NET 8 (`ComposeService` save path, empty-package construction) + React/TS
    (`Spaarke.Compose.Components` client bridge). Understands the unification goal — one operation/patch
    model for both edit-existing and born-in-editor, so there is exactly one byte-author (D5) and no
    parallel full-render export.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A born-in-editor document saves via the Patch Engine as an insert-everything operation set onto an
    empty shadow package; the client `buildContentModel` full-render export path is reconciled/removed so
    both born-in-editor and edit-existing emit the same operation log; no separate full-render export
    path remains; and an empty born-in-editor doc saves as a valid empty shadow package, not a crash.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design §5 (unify born-in-editor into the operation/patch model), owner clarification Q5 ("New docs
      = insert-everything op set onto an empty shadow package; no parallel full-render path"). Spec
      FR-09. As-built inventory: `buildContentModel` full-render export at `docxBridge.ts:397+` is the
      born-in-editor path that "stays, but must feed the SAME operation/patch model, not a parallel
      path." Task 030 built the Patch Engine (the insert path the empty-package op set applies through);
      this task points born-in-editor at it and retires the parallel render export.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs — born-in-editor save path: construct an empty shadow package and apply the insert-everything operation set via `ComposeShadowPatchEngine`</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/utils/docxBridge.ts:397+ — `buildContentModel` full-render path: reconcile so born-in-editor emits the same operation log as edit-existing; remove the parallel export</file>
      <file role="dependency-output">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeShadowPatchEngine.cs — task 030 core (the insert path the op set applies through)</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/design.md §5, Owner Clarification Q5</file>
      <file role="spec">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/spec.md FR-09</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="030" status="pending">`ComposeShadowPatchEngine` core — provides the insert path the empty-package insert-everything op set applies through.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec / FR-09">Born-in-editor documents MUST feed the SAME operation/patch model — initial content = an insert-everything op set onto an empty shadow package. NO separate full-render export path may remain.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / invariants I-1/I-2/I-5">One authoritative model, server-authoritative byte-authoring, one byte-author — the born-in-editor path MUST NOT introduce a second byte-author or a client-side `.docx` build.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Client save/generate fetches use `@spaarke/auth` (`useAuth`/`authenticatedFetch`); no custom token props on the editor.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007 / ADR-013 / NFR-05">The save stays behind `SpeFileStore` (no `Microsoft.Graph` in `Services/Compose/`) and injects no AI internals (Tier-1 NetArchTest green).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038 / NFR-06">The born-in-editor save carries a through-the-wire seam slice (authored/extended in task 034); NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration, or ctor-null tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / §10 Placement Justification">State the Placement Justification in the PR and cite `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`. Run `/conflict-check` before the PR. Report publish size delta vs ~49.63 MB (≤60 MB) + no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Born-in-editor unification onto the operation/patch model; empty-shadow-package construction; client bridge full-render removal; Spaarke auth client contract; BFF hygiene</topic>
    <files>
